 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Axis-Aligned Capsule SDF
-A specialized version where the capsule is aligned with a coordinate axis (e.g., Y-axis). It simplifies the projection step by only clamping the corresponding coordinate [S1, unofficial]. Choose this when rendering static, axis-aligned tubes for performance optimization. See [Axis-Aligned Capsule SDF](link).
+A specialized version where the capsule is aligned with a coordinate axis (e.g., Y-axis) [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from the general form by simplifying the projection step to a single coordinate clamp [S1, unofficial]. Choose it when rendering static, axis-aligned tubes [G]. See [Axis-Aligned Capsule SDF](link).
 
 ### 2D Capsule SDF
-The 2D equivalent, computing distance to a line segment with rounded ends in a plane. Useful for 2D volumetric rendering or sprite-based effects [S5, unofficial]. See [2D Capsule SDF](link).
+The 2D equivalent, computing distance to a line segment with rounded ends in a plane [S5, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from the 3D version by operating in two dimensions for sprite-based or 2D volumetric effects [G]. Choose it for 2D ray marching or procedural 2D geometry [G]. See [2D Capsule SDF](link).
 
